Ugh, that warning label is just going to annoy me more, isn't it. Like I didn't know chocolate's got sugar in it.

I'd grab the Cadbury Dairy Milk. It's mid-afternoon, my legs are wrecked from the intervals, and I'm not paying a quid for a fruit pot that's going to leave me hungry by four. Calories are on the wrap anyway, I can count them myself.

{"choice": 4}

*Stands in front of the machine, half a shift gone, knees aching from the walk.*

Right, I'm not buying the apple and grapes pot, that's just a bit sad after a double shift on the pallets. Probably McCoy's, salt and vinegar, because they're proper crisps and they fill a gap at four o'clock. Doritos are alright but too orange for my liking.

{"choice": 7}

*Snorts at the machine.* Bloody warning labels on the chocolate, as if I didn't know. Mid-afternoon, skint, and I've had nothing but a cup of tea since the telly went on, so I want something that actually fills a gap.

I'm getting the Doritos Tangy Cheese. Crisps, big hit of salt, and it's the one that doesn't need a fork or a fridge. The apple crisps look like something you'd find in a garden centre, and the fruit pots are a waste of a quid when I'm after something proper.

{"choice": 11}

*Sighs and jabs at the machine.* Mid-afternoon, so I'm after something sweet and I can't be arsed with fruit. The warning on the chocolate just reads like a lecture, and every packet has its calories shouted at me in a big badge, which is exactly the talking-down I can't stand. Still, I'll have what I fancy.

I'm going for the Galaxy.

{"choice": 6}

Mid-afternoon at a vending machine, so I'm in the mood for something salty or sweet, nothing fancy. Ha, the beetroot crisps look like something my daughter would photograph for the phone, and I'd rather have a biscuit with my tea than that.

I'm going for the McCoy's. Salt and vinegar, proper crisps, and they don't pretend to be anything else.

{"choice": 9}

Ah, bloody hell, those gruesome photos on everything, I'd never seen one that close before. Put me off the Galaxy straight away.

Right, I'll go for the McCoy's salt and vinegar. I'm not having the yoghurt, Sandra would only say I should have got the posh one anyway. Those crisps are my usual, and I'm not kidding myself they're a health food, but they're a sensible size and I can't be doing with a fruit pot at four o'clock.

{"choice": 8}

*Squints at the warning on the bar.* Oh, here we go, a little black-and-white lecture stuck on the chocolate, like I didn't know chocolate isn't a salad.

I'd really pick the McCoy's. Salt and vinegar, mid-afternoon, job sites have made me sulky and I want something with a bit of bite. I'm not spending money on a fruit pot to feel virtuous when nobody's watching anyway.

{"choice": 2}

*Sighs and squints at the machine.* Honestly, those gruesome pictures on the crisps and chocolate are enough to make you feel like you're being told off by a wagging finger, and I'm not in the mood for that today. The calorie badges on everything just make it all look like homework.

I'd probably go for the Doritos, the Tangy Cheese, because it's what I actually fancy with a cup of tea and I'm not going to pretend otherwise. The blood pressure is supposed to mean I've cut back, but the crisps are still in my glovebox, so there's no point lying to a vending machine.

{"choice": 4}

*Squints at the machine.* Bit of a mouthful on those warning labels, isn't it. Obesity, bowel cancer, heart disease, all in one go, like I'm about to drop dead by the Co-op. And every bar's shouting its calories at me in bold. I'm not counting calories, I'm buying a snack.

Right, I'll have the McCoy's. Salt and vinegar, the proper ones, and they're a good few pence cheaper than the Doritos. Mind you, that's a judgement on price, not on what's good for me, and I'll have the tin of sardines for tea anyway.

{"choice": 11}

Oh, for goodness' sake, look at the state of that machine with its gruesome pictures plastered all over the crisps and chocolate, as if I'm too daft to know a biscuit's bad for me without a photo of somebody's insides.

I'll have the Cadbury Dairy Milk. It's a bit of a treat after the washing and the walk, and I know what it is without being frightened into it.

{"choice": 2}

Half three, standing here with the bus fare already spent, and that warning on the chocolate bars just makes me roll my eyes, they've been slapping that on everything since I was a kid and it hasn't stopped me yet.

I'd go for the McCoy's. Salt and vinegar, cheap, and it's the one thing that actually hits the spot when you've been on your feet since six.

{"choice": 5}

*Squints at the machine, sighs at the gruesome photos stuck on the crisps and bars.* Christ, the bowel one's on the Doritos, nice. Fine, I'm not reading a medical textbook at quarter to four. I want something that'll get me through to half six without me going full zombie on the train home, and I've got about 80p in change.

Honestly, it's the Galaxy. Cheap enough, it's chocolate, and the calorie badge is just another number I'm not going to think about today.

{"choice": 4}

*Glances at the machine, shrugs.* Christ, it's half three and I've been on my feet since quarter to five. Right, what's the warning on the big ones... "excess calories cause obesity" - yeah, I've had that off the GP already, ta. Doesn't stop me wanting a Dairy Milk when I've been shouting at forklifts all day.

I'll have the Galaxy, it's the one I always go for when the shifts have been rubbish, and it's a quid less than the Cadbury in here.

{"choice": 9}
